  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2016-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "With \\(a=\\tfrac12,\\) we have \\(a^{-1}=2.\\) The numerator is \\(2\\cdot2+\\dfrac{2}{2}=4+1=5,\\) and dividing by \\(a=\\tfrac12\\) gives \\(\\dfrac{5}{\\frac{1}{2}}=10.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "\\(a^{-1}=\\frac{1}{a},\\) so \\(a^{-1}=2\\) when \\(a=\\tfrac12\\)",
        "The numerator is \\(2a^{-1}+\\tfrac12 a^{-1}=\\tfrac52 a^{-1};\\) then divide by \\(a\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
